# Python Learning Archive

A public archive of my Python coursework and learning projects. These are historical exercises from my studies, not actively maintained libraries or applications.

The original projects are preserved in separate folders. Their Git commit histories are imported **without squashing**, retaining the original authorship and progression of work.

## Organization

| Directory | Contents | Projects |
| --- | --- | ---: |
| `01-python-fundamentals/` | Python basics, file sorting and the gradual development of a CLI personal helper | 7 |
| `02-python-development/` | Module 2 coursework: packaging, web services, databases, testing and related topics | 15 |
| `03-data-science/` | Module 3 coursework, notebooks and exercises | 12 |

**Total:** 34 original repositories.

Each assignment keeps its original repository name as a subdirectory. Existing project READMEs and source files are preserved.

## A note about the code

These projects document a learning journey. Dependencies may be outdated, some projects may not run without additional setup, and the code does not necessarily represent my current engineering practices.

This archive is for reference and historical context, rather than production use.

## History and attribution

The migration retains the original Git commits, including their authors and timestamps, through history-preserving subtree imports. Other contributors, where present, retain attribution in Git history.

The source repositories will remain available until the archive has been verified. This README may be present before the full import is complete.
